{
  "schema_version": "1.8.0",
  "id": "DHI-ny7t-6ay6-iylf-wn7a",
  "modified": "2026-11-13T19:06:11Z",
  "published": "2026-11-11T17:20:22Z",
  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-42154"
  ],
  "summary": "### Impact",
  "details": "### Impact\r\n\r\nThe remote read endpoint (`/api/v1/read`) does not validate the declared decoded length in a snappy-compressed request body before allocating memory.\r\nAn unauthenticated attacker can send a small payload that causes a huge heap allocation per request. Under concurrent load this can exhaust available memory and crash the Prometheus process.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\n_Has the problem been patched? What versions should users upgrade to?_\r\n\r\nFixed in 3.11.3 and 3.5.3 LTS. Users should upgrade to these versions or later.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\nUser who can not upgrade can place Prometheus behind a reverse proxy or firewall that requires authentication before requests reach /api/v1/read.\r\n\r\n",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
    }
  ],
